      "context": "Screenshot-matched existing crop webpage layout. Scope: freeform quadrilateral crop points, not rectangular resize handles. Point 2 is shown during an independent drag; the other three points stay fixed. Edges follow points live; outside region is masked. Four points are constrained to source bounds and cannot cross. Dragging inside translates the whole selection. Arrow keys nudge the selected point, Esc restores pre-drag position. X/Y edit the selected point; bounds are read-only. PNG output retains transparency outside the polygon. Proposal requires polygon masking support; current rectangular crop implementation does not implement this. Mountain image is a substitute sample; user screenshot photograph was not available as a reusable asset.",
