        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "x39zmU",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 858,
          "name": "01 / Threads — history, new conversation, running",
          "context": "Panel detail flow, 350×596 per state, fits the existing editor at both 1366×768 and 1280×720 without widening the sidebar. Multiple threads can respond concurrently; each thread runs one turn at a time with a FIFO queue. Switching, starting a thread or closing the panel never cancels another run. Threads are scoped to the current blog. New thread is a new conversation, not a new blog. Open rows restore thread-specific messages, partial response, queue, draft attachments and request settings. Replies and queues persist on server across re-entry; reconcile after reconnect before showing Responding. Failure pauses only its own queue. Reply ready is unread, not auto-applied. Review opens selected thread proposals. Applying checks current blog revision; stale proposals require regeneration or explicit review, never overwrite a newer draft silently. Close preserves all threads. Backend parallelism and persistence are requested capabilities, not verified implemented behavior.",
