      "name": "AI CHAT / 09 — Agent outputs · run-linked reports",
      "context": "User direction: Sources is exclusively a read-only index of thread attachments and generated run artifacts. Compact artifact previews live in chat, title/chevron opens exact saved artifact in Sources. Sources tab opens index; index groups Artifacts and Attachments, no mutations. Viewer displays structured output, copy allowed. All sources returns to index; Show message returns to originating chat turn. Review reserved for proposed changes, not report viewing. Filter by current thread; deduplicate by runId/attachmentId. Completed structured runs only in artifact inventory; running/failed status stays in chat. Expired artifacts show unavailable with no dead preview and Show message for recovery. Agent identity metadata remains new proposed contract. Independent validators not exposed in session. Loading correction: no artifact on Send. Starting, working with optional public execution steps, and preparing/persisting remain unboxed activity. Only completed persisted structured results produce a Sources artifact. Failed/cancelled/unknown states are activity + recovery, not report cards. Existing run event union has no granular stage events; phase telemetry is a proposed addition, use generic Working when unavailable. Never expose private reasoning, fabricate progress percentages or use timers to mark steps done. Activity is live-announced politely; reduced motion disables spinner animation. Stop affects this run only, preserves draft/queue, and cancellation races reconcile with server. Manual visual check: no clipping, compact status hierarchy, real next actions. Independent ui_validator/end_user_validator unavailable; validation pending.",
